<section id="intro" class="relative items-center pt-8 pb-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex flex-wrap justify-center">
        <div class="w-full md:w-8/12 lg:w-10/12 xl:w-10/12 px-4 ">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl text-secondary pb-4">
                E-W Framework Coverage, Simplified
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold text-secondary/80 ">
                This Analysis Tool provides a way to profile your data sources to
                measure how well your systems cover the E-W Framework.
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc py-4 pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li>Run automated scans via secure API connections to your Ed-Fi ODS instance.</li>
                <li>Interrogate the data in your CEDS DW through portable SQL queries.</li>
                <li>Manually enter a profile for other data sources.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold text-secondary/80 ">
                The resulting coverage analysis can empower you and your stakeholders to prioritize research
                questions and investment decisions and guide the development of your data systems.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="framework" class="relative items-center pb-24">
    <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex justify-center">
        <div class="w-full md:w-8/12 lg:w-10/12 xl:w-10/12 px-4">
            <div class="pt-32* sm:pt-0">
                <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl text-secondary pb-4">
                    What is the E-W Framework?
                </h2>
                <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold text-secondary/80">
                    The <a href="https://educationtoworkforce.org/" class="link link-hover font-bold hover:text-primary/80">Education-to-Workforce Indicator Framework</a>
                    (or E-W Framework) is an extensive framework developed with input from leading experts from over 20 national and community organizations.
                    It highlights key connections needed between systems to support students as they progress from early education through their career.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex justify-center mt-20">
        <div class="w-full md:w-8/12 lg:w-10/12 xl:w-10/12 px-4">

            <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl text-secondary pb-4">
                The E-W Framework includes
            </h2>

            <ul class="list-disc px-6">
                <li>
                    <h2 class="text-xl mb-4 font-semibold text-secondary">Essential Questions</h2>
                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary">
                        Twenty questions essential for E-W data systems to answer about how students are
                        progressing from early education through career—and using the answers to guide action.
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <h6 class="text-xl mb-4 font-semibold text-secondary">Indicators</h6>
                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary">
                        Student outcomes and milestones and related system conditions
                        associated with economic mobility and security, plus guidance
                        on how to measure them (Metrics).
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <h6 class="text-xl mb-4 font-semibold text-secondary">Disaggregates</h6>
                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary">
                        Characteristics that E-W systems should use to break down
                        data, plus guidance on how to collect them.
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <h6 class="text-xl mb-4 font-semibold text-secondary">Evidence-Based Practices</h6>
                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary">
                        The framework is centered around equity-based
                        principles and also provides evidence based practices.
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex justify-center mt-8 ">
        <div class="w-full md:w-10/12 xl:w-8/12 px-4 ">
            <img src="images/ew-diagram.png" class="w-full align-middle shadow rounded-lg bg-white p-5"
                 alt="A depiction of the E-W Framework components,
                        such as Essential Questions and Evidence-based practices,
                        and the general lifecycle of how they are interacted with" />
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="tool" class="relative items-center pb-24">
    <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex flex-wrap justify-center">
        <div class="w-full md:w-8/12 lg:w-10/12 xl:w-10/12 px-4 ">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl text-secondary pb-4">
                What does the E-W Analysis Tool do?
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold text-secondary/80">
                This Analysis Tool was developed by Double Line to build upon the rich information in the
                E-W Framework and enable you to understand which indicators your data systems cover.
                It then calculates coverage of the recommended metrics for each Indicator,
                giving you a visual representation of your framework coverage by Indicator and by Essential Question.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
